WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:04.681
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, hopefully you’ve
all had a chance to watch some of my comic

00:00:04.681 --> 00:00:10.420
con videos.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:16.560
I asked everyone on twitter which new footage
they wanted me to do a breakdown for and Age

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.560
of Ultron won as expected.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.980
There were a ton of new trailers, so at the
end of this video I’ll explain which other

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.840
ones I’m going to be doing.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.230
And I’ll announce who won my Marvel giveaway.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:31.550
Hello to any new people, if you just found
me because of all the comic con stuff I do

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.040
weekly Marvel videos.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.280
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.570
This week Guardians of The Galaxy is in theaters,
it’s going to be awesome, so I’ll be doing

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.810
a bunch of separate videos for that.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:41.630
Plus they already confirmed a sequel for 2017.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:45.740
But let’s talk about that Avengers 2 trailer.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.750
In case you didn’t see it, it ended up being
pretty close to the scene I described in an

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.750
old video from a couple weeks ago.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.750
It was the party scene in the Avengers Tower.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.200
The clip at comic con had a bunch of new stuff
in it though.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:05.700
I know a lot of you have asked about the actual
footage and no I can’t just post the trailer.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:06.700
It’s super illegal.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.450
Those people that leaked the Deadpool test
footage and the Batman vs Superman clip.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.670
Fox, Marvel and Warner Brothers are going
to throw them into a deep dark pit.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:21.299
Marvel was really nice and released a bunch
of images, so when I’m talking about the

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:22.649
footage I’ll use those.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:38.200
First we saw the Party Scene.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.409
It’s a fully operational Avengers Tower.

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:43.109
It’s sick how awesome it looks.

00:01:43.109 --> 00:01:44.109
If you remember, Tony Stark and Pepper Potts
were looking at blueprints of it at the end

00:01:44.109 --> 00:01:45.189
of the first Avengers movie.

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:48.060
So this is what the floorplan is.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.140
All of the avengers including Thor are living
on earth full time.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.579
Guardians of the Galaxy happens about 6 months
earlier in the timeline, but they haven’t

00:01:57.579 --> 00:01:59.209
interacted with the Avengers yet.

00:01:59.209 --> 00:02:00.969
I repeat yet.

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:05.149
What’s been happening since Winter Soldier
is that the Avengers have been cleaning up

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:12.750
the Hydra Labs, like the one Baron Von Strucker
was in with Quicksilver, Scarlet Witch and

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.400
Loki’s staff.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.890
Because HYDRA was so embedded in the organizations
of the world, the day to day grind of cleaning

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:24.659
up all the remnants has gotten too exhausting
and to maximize efficiency and vacation time.

00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:25.890
Tony Stark creates Ultron.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:31.459
He’s like an 8 foot tall robot built from
modified elements of Iron Man suits.

00:02:31.459 --> 00:02:35.580
But he has a new AI system capable of learning.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.570
Skynet Terminator style.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:42.390
Ultron’s mission parameters as defined by
Tony Stark are to eradicate evil and make

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.510
the world a better place.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.370
Cue scary music.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:49.610
Because of the way machines think, the cold
efficiency and because of Tony Stark’s loose

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.549
language in eradicating evil.

00:02:52.549 --> 00:02:57.290
Ultron determines that humans are the problem
and for the good of the planet.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:58.620
They need to be eliminated.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:04.269
Thus Ultron begins his war against the Avengers,
armed with his own army of Ultron replicants.

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:09.999
The Avengers Trailer goes from this party
scene with all of them laughing taking turns

00:03:09.999 --> 00:03:16.751
trying to pick up Thor’s hammer but only
Captain America is able to make it budge,

00:03:16.751 --> 00:03:17.751
just a little.

00:03:17.751 --> 00:03:21.010
During that scene, everyone in the audience
went crazy.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:25.200
In the comics Captain America has used Thor’s
hammer, but he’s never done it on screen.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.580
So you guys will go nuts when you actually
see it in the movie.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:35.709
Ultron busts in during the party and says
“There is one path to peace, Your extinction”

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:37.660
and opens fire on them.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.489
Then it cuts to a montage of WTF action scenes.

00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:48.620
Explosions all over the world, Bruce Banner
in the woods, tanks fighting in the snow.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.239
Tony Stark has this line where he says, “It’s
the end, the end of the path I started us

00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:53.239
on.”

00:03:53.239 --> 00:03:55.340
and Black Widow says “Nothing lasts forever”.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.540
Then in a different scene Tony is fighting
the Hulk in his Hulkbuster armor.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:03.799
This is the concept art, but here’s a look
at a prop replica of the arm.

00:04:03.799 --> 00:04:05.359
Freaking awesome right?

00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:08.920
Then it cuts to a scene of Ultron saying,
“Look, no string on me.”

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:15.909
- you have to picture James Spader saying
it in his creepy Blacklist voice.

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:19.769
It’s basically that, processed to sound
more like a machine voice, like JARVIS.

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:24.919
Then it ends with a scene of Tony in a wasteland
of battle debris with all the other Avengers

00:04:24.919 --> 00:04:26.930
lying on the ground like they just got the
shit beaten out of them.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.680
Even Captain America’s shield is cracked.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.080
Here’s a shot of the prop in real life.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.139
It’s the scene that happens after this promo
image.

00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:41.100
The big posters they revealed over the course
of the weekend.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:46.110
They went up against Ultron and his army and
got their asses handed to them.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:49.830
Andy Serkis appeared briefly in the background
of a battle scene.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:54.340
It was super quick, but it was live action,
meaning he wasn’t a mo-cap creature and

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.800
he was most definitely evil.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:03.330
So when you theorycraft who he’s playing,
think of human villains in the Marvel universe.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.040
I don’t think it’s MODOK or anything.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:12.250
That’s more of an old Patton Oswalt joke.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:16.020
That’s pretty much it.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:23.490
But you’ve seen what Ultron looks like in
his final form.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:29.330
This poster isn’t what he first looks like
when tony stark builds him.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:32.510
Before he rebels he looks more like an Iron
Man suit.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:36.180
One of the first things Joss Whedon explained
about Ultron was that we would see him evolve

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.699
mentally throughout the film and physically
as he upgrades himself.

00:05:39.699 --> 00:05:43.720
If you guys watched the panel footage I uploaded,
when Josh Brolin came out with the Infinity

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:44.720
Gauntlet.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:45.720
It made me think.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.520
What if Thanos steps in to help for a price.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:51.569
Like bargaining the tesseract for his assistance.

00:05:51.569 --> 00:05:53.830
Of course Vision will be the one to finally
take Ultron on directly.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:59.300
He’s explained as the good son of Tony Stark,
Ultron being the Bad Son.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:03.490
So think of Avengers 2 as a story about two
brothers, Ultron and Vision.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.620
Like Cain and Abel in the biblical sense.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.819
Except the ending is different.

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:09.960
Everyone was a little disappointed that Marvel
didn’t roll out a Tom Hiddleston level opening

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.629
at their panel.

00:06:12.629 --> 00:06:19.950
They have 6 new mystery films and didn’t
announce what any of them were.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.479
I think there are a couple big reasons why,
mostly all practical.

00:06:22.479 --> 00:06:27.500
The biggest is that they have a ton of unsigned
deals with actors, writers and directors for

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:28.500
all those films.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.949
And until all those people sign ink on paper.

00:06:31.949 --> 00:06:35.180
Those films could change.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:37.450
Think about Ant Man.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:41.680
A bunch of people just dropped out of the
movie, the script isn’t finished and they

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:42.680
start shooting in August.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:43.680
That’s only a couple weeks away.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.650
That’s how far behind they are.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:46.669
Joaquin Phoenix was the newest rumor for Doctor
Strange.

00:06:46.669 --> 00:06:47.669
As weird as that choice sounds it doesn’t
matter.

00:06:47.669 --> 00:06:48.669
No one they’ve offered the part to has signed
a contract.

00:06:48.669 --> 00:06:49.669
And it’s the same story for all those other
movies.

00:06:49.669 --> 00:06:53.539
The other big reason why they didn’t tease
phase 3 stuff is Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:06:53.539 --> 00:06:55.599
It’s being released this week.

00:06:55.599 --> 00:06:59.759
And if they talked about too many other films,
they’d steal a lot of thunder from it.

00:06:59.759 --> 00:07:04.569
So they wanted to promote it more than they
wanted to promote a movie coming out in 4

00:07:04.569 --> 00:07:05.569
years.

00:07:05.569 --> 00:07:08.080
It sucks that they didn’t confirm anything,
but they did drop Guardians 2.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.310
That’s being released July 28th 2017.

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:15.189
James Gunn had already said he’d direct
the sequel if the first one did well enough.

00:07:15.189 --> 00:07:18.229
And based on projections and early ticket
sales, it totally will.

00:07:18.229 --> 00:07:24.139
Looking back on the weekend I still think
the Marvel panel was the best, with the Batman

00:07:24.139 --> 00:07:27.610
vs Superman Warner Bros panel being a close
second.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:39.430
Michael Douglas old-mansplaining Ant Man was
a bit of a drag, but he’s Michael Douglas,

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.430
what do you expect?

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:44.350
I’ll be doing a bunch of separate Guardians
videos for that movie this week including

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:48.099
a review and a Guardians 2 video with all
the stories I think they should do.

00:07:48.099 --> 00:07:49.099
Be sure to subscribe to get all that stuff.

00:07:49.099 --> 00:07:50.979
Really the big tease is them bringing Nova
into the movie.

00:07:50.979 --> 00:07:53.860
That’s really the next big step for that
franchise.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.960
And deepening the Thanos lore in preparation
for Avengers 3.

